{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"compacted_at":1787314874387200001,"compiled_state":{"alias":"tireless-convenable-canvasback","assignee":null,"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","authorship":{"signed":3,"unsigned":0},"authorship_ledger":[{"content_hash":"09cb782b20195c5a4d954cd31f80267e059b0bfd5dc0d591940077f81b8ec005","event_uuid":"6a4f01ce-65b4-4896-a099-3d031c786340","position":{"commit_sha":"a1b688b1b3b2a7326bc798edc488df03c49a17d4","position":"1787312653860522001-6a4f01ce-65b4-4896-a099-3d031c786340"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"f7fa25f7c9459f864b6d0f54af030fd077858e2255b116d2338559257a7fd986","event_uuid":"2a892a1e-7c7a-4ed4-b434-bc77a1bee77d","position":{"commit_sha":"7154b1a21ccdc520290add9cc2e07e940c0849ca","position":"1787312674910364001-2a892a1e-7c7a-4ed4-b434-bc77a1bee77d"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"8412b75ff846e366990fb342bca39bbca948f0c9158d60e668f3234bd0f53a34","event_uuid":"8f40ecdb-2174-46f2-ad6b-6fa4e18f061f","position":{"commit_sha":"1a4e3d7264c25265e1c3f5c158a63656897f0cbb","position":"1787312684577448001-8f40ecdb-2174-46f2-ad6b-6fa4e18f061f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[],"created_at":1787312653860522001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"2a892a1e-7c7a-4ed4-b434-bc77a1bee77d","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"f400-987f-45f6-419a"},{"link_uuid":"8f40ecdb-2174-46f2-ad6b-6fa4e18f061f","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"958e-f4b3-275c-4154"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\n`958e-f4b3-275c-4154` made the write-path drain gate O(1) on a **quiet** store by caching\n\"nothing can be pending before T\" in `.rebar/enrich-gate.json`. The marker is only ever\n*written* on a scan that found nothing:\n\n```python\n# src/rebar/llm/overlap/queue.py:374-377\nif out:\n    _clear_gate_marker(tracker)\nelse:\n    _write_gate_marker(tracker, now_ns, soonest)\n```\n\nSo a **single** pending entry is enough to disable the fast path for the entire store, and every\nsubsequent write pays a full walk of every ticket directory until the pending set empties again.\n\n## Measured (2026-08-21, synthetic stores, marker forced cold)\n\n| store size | pending | gate ms |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1000 | 1 | 116.9 |\n| 1000 | 500 | 157.1 |\n| 1000 | 1000 | 206.5 |\n| 4000 | 1 | 560.3 |\n| 4000 | 500 | 572.3 |\n| 4000 | 0 | cold 525.7, **warm 0.110** |\n\n- Cost is **linear in store size** (x4 tickets -> x3.6-4.8) and only weakly sensitive to backlog\n  depth (x500 depth -> x1.34; x1000 -> x1.77).\n- **Depth 1 already costs the full scan.** The trigger is binary, not proportional.\n- The marker, when it engages, is ~4,800x faster (0.110 ms vs 525.7 ms).\n\nOn the live 4,938-ticket store this is 1,200-1,330 ms per write.\n\n## Why this is filed separately\n\nFound while debugging `f400-987f-45f6-419a` (\"deep enrichment backlog starves late entries\").\nThat bug's mechanism is the **selection order** (an id-sorted prefix); this one is the **marker's\nall-or-nothing design**. They share a precondition (a non-empty pending set) but are distinct\nmechanisms, proven by the table above: fixing fairness lets *that* store's backlog drain to\nempty, which restores the marker there, but it does not help any store that keeps one entry\npending. Folding a marker redesign into a bug fix would exceed that bug's authorised scope, so\nit is recorded here instead.\n\n## Scope note (read before implementing)\n\n`958e`'s own block comment (`queue.py:232-254`) enumerates three accepted failure modes and all\nthree are the marker wrongly saying *quiet*. The branch that never writes the marker at all is\nimplemented but discussed nowhere — not in the comment, not in the commit message, and not in\nany of the 9 marker tests, every one of which seeds a store whose pending set becomes empty.\n\nNote also that story `c1de-d6a0-6cef-4135`'s AC scopes the budget to the quiet case: *\"`maybe_drain`\nno-ops with no spawn **when nothing soaked**, within `DRAIN_GATE_BUDGET_MS` (20 ms)\"*. A gate that\nfinds a real backlog is not on that no-op path, so this is a **cost/design** improvement, not a\nviolated contract — size it accordingly.\n\n`f400`'s open question #3 sketches the candidate direction: record \"nothing pending BEFORE\nindex N\" rather than all-or-nothing. That is a **design change**, so it wants a plan and a\nreview, not a drive-by patch.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] A store with a standing non-empty pending set does not pay a full store walk on every write.\n- [ ] The existing marker honesty rules are preserved: the cache can still only ever say\n      \"nothing is pending\" (never manufacture one), every queue append still invalidates it, and\n      it is still TTL-bounded.\n- [ ] A test seeds a store with a **permanently non-empty** pending set and pins the gate cost\n      (by probe/syscall count, not wall clock — `check_wall_clock_asserts`).\n- [ ] `make lint`, `make typecheck`, and the unit sweep are green.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"undeclared","keyring":[],"managed_refs":[["relates_to","958e-f4b3-275c-4154"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"","plan_review_phase":"planning","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"open","tags":[],"ticket_id":"4144-75d3-6af1-47d3","ticket_type":"bug","title":"enrich gate marker is all-or-nothing: one pending entry disables the O(1) fast path store-wide","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["6a4f01ce-65b4-4896-a099-3d031c786340","2a892a1e-7c7a-4ed4-b434-bc77a1bee77d","8f40ecdb-2174-46f2-ad6b-6fa4e18f061f"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787314874387200001,"uuid":"77e1c862-851a-40e2-8d6a-7494dbcbd0c3"}